<refentry id="gmime-building">
  <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>Compiling the GMime libraries</refentrytitle>
    <manvolnum>3</manvolnum>
    <refmiscinfo>GMime Library</refmiscinfo>
  </refmeta>
  <refnamediv>
    <refname>Compiling the GMime Libraries</refname>
    <refpurpose>How to compile GMime itself</refpurpose>
  </refnamediv>
  <refsect1 id="dependencies">
    <title>Dependencies</title>
    <para>
      GMime 4 uses Meson 1.3.0 or newer and Ninja. A C compiler,
      pkg-config, GLib, GObject, GIO, and GThread 2.88.0 or newer, zlib,
      and iconv are required. On systems without iconv in the C library,
      install GNU libiconv.
    </para>
    <para>
      GPGME 1.6.0 or newer and libgpg-error provide optional OpenPGP and
      S/MIME support. Libidn2 2.0.0 or newer provides optional IDN
      conversion; GLib is used when libidn2 is disabled or unavailable.
      GObject introspection and vapigen provide optional language bindings.
      The API reference requires gtk-doc and DocBook tools.
    </para>
  </refsect1>
  <refsect1 id="building">
    <title>Building and testing GMime</title>
    <para>
      Builds use a separate build directory. The same commands work
      for a Git checkout or an unpacked source archive:
    </para>
    <programlisting>
meson setup _build --prefix=/usr/local
meson compile -C _build
meson test -C _build --print-errorlogs
meson install -C _build
    </programlisting>
    <para>
      Installation may require elevated permissions when the prefix is
      a system directory. Packagers can stage installation with
      <literal>meson install -C _build --destdir DESTDIR</literal>.
      Verify the installed package with
      <literal>pkg-config --modversion gmime-4.0</literal>.
    </para>
    <para>
      Use <literal>meson configure _build</literal> to inspect options.
      Configuration diagnostics are in
      <filename>_build/meson-logs/meson-log.txt</filename>, and test
      output is in <filename>_build/meson-logs/testlog.txt</filename>.
      Crypto tests additionally need GnuPG and the supplied test keys.
      Preserve the repository line endings in test fixtures.
    </para>
  </refsect1>
  <refsect1 id="extra-configuration-options">
    <title>Configuration options</title>
    <para>
      The <literal>crypto</literal>, <literal>libidn</literal>,
      <literal>introspection</literal>, and <literal>vapi</literal>
      options accept <literal>auto</literal> (the default),
      <literal>enabled</literal>, or <literal>disabled</literal>.
      Enabled features require their dependencies; auto features are
      built when their dependencies are available. Vala bindings require
      introspection, which requires a shared library.
    </para>
    <programlisting>
meson setup _build -Dcrypto=enabled -Dlibidn=enabled
meson configure _build -Dgtk_doc=true
meson compile -C _build gmime-doc
    </programlisting>
    <para>
      Disable test programs with <literal>-Dtests=false</literal> and
      examples with <literal>-Dexamples=false</literal>. Enable runtime
      warnings about malformed MIME with <literal>-Dmime_warnings=true</literal>.
      Meson's standard options support static builds
      (<literal>-Ddefault_library=static</literal>), coverage
      (<literal>-Db_coverage=true</literal>), and sanitizers
      (<literal>-Db_sanitize=address,undefined</literal>).
    </para>
    <para>
      When cross-compiling without an executable wrapper, the iconv
      detector cannot run and the built-in platform charset aliases
      are used instead.
    </para>
  </refsect1>
</refentry>
